  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests pass now (2 of 2).\n\nThe bug was in `src/vat.js`. `withVat` used `Math.floor(pence * 1.2)`, which rounds down. The comment and the test both say the result should round to the nearest penny. For 999 pence, 999 × 1.2 = 1198.8, so the function returned 1198 when it should return 1199. I changed `Math.floor` to `Math.round` on that one line.\n\nI didn't commit the change, since you didn't ask for a commit.",
